<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="csrf-token" content="{{ csrf_token() }}"><title>Laravel Resumable Uploads</title>@vite(['resources/css/app.css','resources/js/app.js'])</head>
<body><main class="shell"><nav><a class="brand" href="/">LRU<span>.</span></a><span>Resumable upload systems demo</span></nav>
<section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Laravel 12 · Queue-backed · SHA-256 verified</p><h1>Large uploads that<br><em>pick up where they left off.</em></h1><p class="lede">Pause the browser, lose the network, or restart the worker—the server keeps an exact record of every verified byte.</p></div><div class="proof"><strong>8 MiB</strong><span>default chunks</span><strong>10 GiB</strong><span>demo limit</span><strong>O(1)</strong><span>assembly memory</span></div></section>
<section class="uploader" id="dropzone"><input id="file" type="file" hidden><div class="empty" id="empty"><div class="upload-icon">↑</div><h2>Choose a large file</h2><p>or drop it here · any file up to 10 GiB</p><button id="choose">Select file</button> <button id="resume" class="secondary" hidden>Resume saved upload</button></div><div class="active" id="active" hidden><div class="file-row"><div class="file-icon">FILE</div><div class="file-meta"><strong id="filename"></strong><span id="filesize"></span></div><span class="badge" id="badge">Hashing</span></div><div class="meter"><i id="bar"></i></div><div class="stats"><span id="status">Calculating SHA-256…</span><strong id="percent">0%</strong></div><div class="actions"><button id="pause" class="secondary">Pause</button><button id="cancel" class="danger">Cancel upload</button></div><pre id="detail"></pre></div></section>
<section class="architecture"><p class="eyebrow">What this proves</p><h2>Small requests. Durable state. Bounded memory.</h2><div class="cards"><article><b>01</b><h3>Verify each chunk</h3><p>Every request carries a SHA-256. Duplicate chunks are idempotent; conflicting bytes are rejected.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h3>Resume precisely</h3><p>The browser asks for missing indexes and skips bytes already accepted by the server.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h3>Assemble off-request</h3><p>A retry-safe queue job streams chunks, verifies the digest, and publishes atomically.</p></article></div></section></main><footer>Built as an interview-sized systems demo · Laravel Resumable Uploads</footer></body></html>
